WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.821
When Pollyanna arrived, Miss Polly was reading in her sitting room.

2
00:00:16.902 --> 00:00:20.764
She didn't bother to stand up but extended a hand for Pollyanna to shake.

3
00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:23.025
"How do you do, Pollyanna?

4
00:00:23.045 --> 00:00:28.167
I—" Pollyanna raced across the room and threw her arms around her startled relative.

5
00:00:28.187 --> 00:00:30.488
"Aunt Polly!

6
00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.345
I'm so glad you're letting me live with you!"

7
00:00:36.166 --> 00:00:40.227
Pollyanna sobbed with relief, burying her face in Aunt Polly's lap.

8
00:00:40.247 --> 00:00:43.348
"I'm sure that's true."

9
00:00:44.368 --> 00:00:47.309
Aunt Polly tried to loosen Pollyanna's grip around her waist.

10
00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:50.790
"Please be good enough to stand up straight.

11
00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.051
I don't even know what you look like."

12
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:55.351
Pollyanna stood up at once.

13
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.041
"I should explain why I'm wearing red instead of black.

14
00:01:03.401 --> 00:01:08.603
I told Nancy how Father said—" "Never mind what he said," Aunt Polly interrupted.

15
00:01:08.623 --> 00:01:11.425
"You've brought a trunk, I assume?"

16
00:01:11.445 --> 00:01:13.325
"Yes, indeed.

17
00:01:13.686 --> 00:01:15.526
I don't have many things of my own.

18
00:01:16.347 --> 00:01:20.708
But the Ladies' Aiders thought I should bring Father's books and—" "Pollyanna!"

19
00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:22.449
Aunt Polly interrupted again.

20
00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:25.270
"There's something we should get straight right away.

21
00:01:26.111 --> 00:01:29.152
I don't want to hear anything about your father."

22
00:01:30.776 --> 00:01:32.077
Pollyanna looked startled.

23
00:01:32.097 --> 00:01:35.819
"You mean nothing at all?"

24
00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:41.883
"It's time to go upstairs to your room," Aunt Polly said, changing the subject.

25
00:01:43.024 --> 00:01:45.826
Silently, Pollyanna followed her aunt from the sitting room.

26
00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:51.089
Her eyes were filled with tears, but she bravely held her chin high.

27
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.352
She thought Aunt Polly was probably being kind.

28
00:01:56.452 --> 00:02:00.495
"I'm glad Aunt Polly doesn't want to talk about Father," Pollyanna thought.

29
00:02:00.515 --> 00:02:04.618
"Maybe if I don't talk about him, I won't miss him so much."

30
00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:11.643
They were in an upstairs hallway now, and Pollyanna eagerly admired the thick rugs and pictures in gold

31
00:02:11.703 --> 00:02:20.389
frames. Open doors offered glimpses into beautifully furnished bedrooms with lace curtains at the windows.

32
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.152
Pollyanna couldn't wait to see which bedroom was hers.

33
00:02:25.252 --> 00:02:28.553
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you have so many pretty things.

34
00:02:29.694 --> 00:02:31.375
You must be glad you're rich!"

35
00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:32.915
Pollyanna exclaimed.

36
00:02:32.935 --> 00:02:36.457
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly scolded.

37
00:02:36.477 --> 00:02:40.338
"We do not talk about money in this family!"

38
00:02:41.359 --> 00:02:45.621
Aunt Polly's instinct had been to put her niece as far away from herself as possible.

39
00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:49.822
She knew children were careless, so the attic was perfect.

40
00:02:50.663 --> 00:02:53.364
It contained nothing valuable that Pollyanna could ruin.

41
00:02:54.348 --> 00:02:59.510
Now that Aunt Polly had met Pollyanna, she'd seen that this girl was very interested in money and

42
00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.852
possessions. Her instinct had been right!

43
00:03:05.573 --> 00:03:09.975
Aunt Polly opened a door, and they went upstairs into the dim, hot attic.

44
00:03:12.696 --> 00:03:17.278
Pollyanna couldn't imagine why Aunt Polly was taking her someplace where it was hard to breathe.

45
00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:21.560
"Here's your room," Aunt Polly said, opening a door.

46
00:03:23.048 --> 00:03:24.749
"I see Tom has brought up your trunk.

47
00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:25.990
Do you have the key?"

48
00:03:27.311 --> 00:03:28.192
Pollyanna nodded.

49
00:03:29.232 --> 00:03:30.914
Her eyes were wide with fright.

50
00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:36.357
"When I ask a question, Pollyanna, I'd like you to speak."

51
00:03:36.377 --> 00:03:38.599
"Yes, Aunt Polly."

52
00:03:38.619 --> 00:03:40.881
"Thank you, that's better."

53
00:03:42.382 --> 00:03:45.264
Aunt Polly glanced at the water pitcher, which Nancy had filled.

54
00:03:45.284 --> 00:03:48.326
"I believe you have everything you need.

55
00:03:49.346 --> 00:03:51.228
I'll send Nancy to help you unpack.

56
00:03:52.228 --> 00:03:53.648
Supper is at six o'clock."

57
00:03:55.949 --> 00:03:59.290
Aunt Polly abruptly went downstairs, leaving Pollyanna alone.

58
00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.431
When Nancy came up a few minutes later, she found Pollyanna sobbing.

59
00:04:04.451 --> 00:04:08.432
"Oh, you poor lamb!"

60
00:04:09.493 --> 00:04:11.493
Nancy dropped to the floor and hugged Pollyanna.

61
00:04:11.513 --> 00:04:14.394
"Let's hang up your dresses."

62
00:04:14.414 --> 00:04:17.615
"I don't have many."

63
00:04:17.635 --> 00:04:21.076
"Then it'll be a quick job," Nancy said.

64
00:04:22.188 --> 00:04:23.609
Pollyanna suddenly smiled.

65
00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.893
"Well, I can be glad about that!"

66
00:04:28.454 --> 00:04:29.955
Nancy didn't know how to respond.

67
00:04:31.577 --> 00:04:35.360
She quickly unpacked Pollyanna's patched underwear and out-of-style dresses.

68
00:04:36.602 --> 00:04:39.444
Nancy suspected they'd all come from the donation box.

69
00:04:39.464 --> 00:04:46.010
"This will be a nice room," Pollyanna said, looking out a window.

70
00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.372
"Don't you think?

71
00:04:48.596 --> 00:04:52.238
I'm glad there isn't a mirror because now I can't see my freckles.

72
00:04:53.439 --> 00:04:56.961
And the view from this window is better than any picture.

73
00:04:58.121 --> 00:05:01.003
I'm so glad Aunt Polly let me have this room!"

74
00:05:02.184 --> 00:05:06.526
To Pollyanna's surprise, Nancy stifled a sob and ran downstairs.

75
00:05:12.369 --> 00:05:17.112
Left alone, Pollyanna opened the window and let in the cool, fresh air along with some flies.

76
00:05:18.856 --> 00:05:21.759
She smiled mischievously as she studied the tree outside.

77
00:05:21.779 --> 00:05:26.763
"I bet I could climb down this tree!"

78
00:05:29.405 --> 00:05:33.008
An hour later the hall clock struck six, and Nancy rang the bell for supper.

79
00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.692
Five minutes passed, and there was no sign of Pollyanna.

80
00:05:40.054 --> 00:05:42.736
Aunt Polly stepped into the hall and listened intently.

81
00:05:43.897 --> 00:05:46.780
For a moment she waited, tapping her foot impatiently.

82
00:05:48.461 --> 00:05:50.112
Then she swept into the dining room.
